            "status": "succeeded",
            "output": "Review (request 5d7d53): `/` binds tighter than `-`, so this computes `(sum(xs) / len(xs)) - 1`, which is the mean minus 1 and not the mean. It also raises ZeroDivisionError on an empty list.\n\nSuggested fix (from the sub-task delegated to carol/claude):\n\n    def mean(xs): return sum(xs) / len(xs)\n\nIf you need empty input handled: `def mean(xs): return sum(xs) / len(xs) if xs else float('nan')`. If you meant an n−1 denominator, that belongs in sample variance, not the mean, and needs parentheses: `/ (len(xs) - 1)`."
          },
