            "status": "succeeded",
            "output": "Corrected:\n\n    def mean(xs): return sum(xs) / len(xs)\n\nWhy: `/` binds tighter than `-`, so the original computes `(sum(xs) / len(xs)) - 1`, which is the mean minus 1. The arithmetic mean is just sum / count, so the `- 1` should go.\n\nIf you meant the n−1 (Bessel) denominator, that applies to sample variance, not the mean. In that case you'd need parentheses: `sum(...) / (len(xs) - 1)`.\n\nOptional version that also handles empty input:\n\n    def mean(xs): return sum(xs) / len(xs) if xs else float('nan')"
          },
